That's true. I think that's, isn't that how Legend of Zelda started?

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.220
Yeah. The guy in the cave, he's your uncle's lawyer.

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:49.000
The guy in the cave, he said, yeah, it's dangerous to go alone.

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:50.780
Your uncle died. Take $500,000.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:55.020
Yeah. It was mistranslated in the North American version.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:01.720
Really makes you question the intentions of the title Wall Street Kid though, right?

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:11.820
Like, did you guys must've thought, or at least I definitely thought that you'd be playing as like a kid who's gonna do like some fun Wall Street style shanigans.

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:13.120
But instead, you're just-

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:18.680
You could be like running through the like floor, like knocking people over as they're like, as they're like playing the stock market.

00:01:18.680 --> 00:01:20.200
I would've been here for it.

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:31.180
But even just like a kid's perspective of the stock market, which maybe this game is, but like, you know, like you're not a kid in the game, but you are, I guess, a-

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:32.260
You're like a relative kid.

00:01:32.420 --> 00:01:35.200
You're like your 20s. Yeah, you're a novice in the Wall Street.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:41.140
Yeah. You're not like some hedge fund guy who already knows the ins and outs of the market.

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:45.240
You've just acquired a large inheritance.

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:46.480
How large, Sean?

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:58.060
Oh, it's $600 billion, which I'm pretty sure would make you the richest person in the world in today's money.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:01.220
Especially in 1990 money.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:04.500
Oh, yeah. Yeah, they future-proofed that for a while.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:07.040
Yeah. But here's the thing.

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:14.060
You can only get the $600 billion inheritance according to the will if you prove yourself.

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:17.240
Yeah. Which is crazy, right?

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:27.920
Yeah, at a certain point, if you're like a hundred billionaire, does the ability to like work with millions of dollars even translate at all to what your life would be like as a hundred billionaire?

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:33.300
I don't think it's- I think it's a different kind of wealth at that point.

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:41.360
Yeah. So it would be like saying like, oh, before you can earn this million dollars, let's see how you spend this nickel.

00:02:42.860 --> 00:02:44.420
It doesn't really translate.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:51.700
Right. I agree with you. And not even like, let's see how you would use the money or let's see if you're financially responsible.

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:58.260
It's just, you have seven days to, or maybe it's 14 days, to double your money.

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:01.220
You've got a month. I'm going to give you $500,000.

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:03.380
Well, they start asking you about the house pretty early.

00:03:03.520 --> 00:03:07.200
They do. But you don't need to say yes.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:09.180
You get a month. Right. Okay.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:18.240
That's actually a good strategy for the players at home because it took me a couple of resets to get to the point where I could afford the house in time before the game over.

00:03:18.440 --> 00:03:20.060
But let's not jump into-

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:21.000
Yeah, don't jump in there.

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:24.120
Shit. Instead, just think about the proposition for a second.

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:29.280
So the game starts off by telling you, your uncle's lawyer tells you your uncle died.

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:32.720
Uh-huh. He had a $600 billion inheritance that he's going to give to you.

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:43.120
Only if you can turn $500,000 into a million dollars, but not like to do anything else other than to buy a million dollar house.

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:51.440
So the only way to do that is not to start a small business or go on Shark Tank and pitch an idea.

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:53.980
It's just play the stock market.

